ade was that  lindsay's actions are protected under  these constitutional safeguards for  members of congress not getting punished  for their speech or actions performed in  the course of their legislative duties  so to explain that in layman's terms  the lawyers for lindsay said when  lindsay called  to inquire about those election results  he was performing legislative duties as  a senator of the united states  that probably sounds like bs to you and  it is and both the d.a and the judge  said  graham isn't a georgia resident and  graham is not a georgia politician  and u.s senators  don't have any legitimate congressional  function in personally calling state  election officials to argue about the  results or to suggest that the results  might be wrong it's it doesn't make any  sense it's not an art but as a senator  he has no role there he has no standing  he's not a voter so he can't use that  argument what he was doing was he was  trying to trade on his name and  influence by calling and saying hey this  is lindsey graham i'm a u.s senator i'm  paying attention to what you're doing  don't you think maybe you could review  the results and maybe see if they  weren't right but there was no  legitimate legislative function as a us  senator being served there and  unfortunately the judge agreed with that  you don't get to choose which laws you  would like to follow  i mean sometimes these people in power  do but you shouldn't get to anyway and  lindsey graham at least for now and  we'll see if he  appeals the decision if it's subject to  appeal or what he tries to do between  now and august 2nd in principle he is  supposed to show up and testify on  august 2nd i know that clearly his  lawyers don't want him to that's why  they tried every possible argument to  get him out of it and if indeed he does  testify it should be absolutely  fascinating we will have the clips and  more of the stories that we talked about  in this segment on the david pakman show  instagram 